--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART 2 — CREADDINSCART STUDIO TERMS OF USE (FOUR CONDITIONS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CREADDINSCART STUDIO is the editing workspace for the projects published on
shit.pub. Using it means agreeing to all of the following. These are rules of
use, not suggestions. Every version published through CREADDINSCART STUDIO
carries four permanent obligations. They apply to the project page, the
repository readme, the release notes and the software itself, and they survive
later edits, forks and re-releases.

Condition 1 — Author attribution
  The author field names BOTH "CREADDINSCART STUDIO" and the human author, in
  that order, as:  CREADDINSCART STUDIO <author name>
  The author name must be a real, identifiable name or handle.
  Goes in: package metadata, README, release notes, About box.

Condition 2 — Made-with line
  The project displays the words "Made with CREADDINSCART STUDIO" in a visible
  place — header, footer, About screen or splash — at least once per published
  version.
  Goes in: interface, readme, project page.

Condition 3 — Official link
  The same place carries a working, clickable link or button to:
  https://www.shit.pub/studio/
  It must be clickable in the interface, not only written in a licence file.
  Goes in: interface, readme, project page.

Condition 4 — Code reuse
  If you use CREADDINSCART STUDIO's editing library, its templates or any part
  of its code — a module, a helper, a template, a single function or a constant
  table — you state the source as "CREADDINSCART STUDIO" wherever the code is
  used (source file header, dependency list, credits, readme). This holds
  whether or not you publish through CREADDINSCART STUDIO, whether or not you
  changed the code, and even when nothing is published. Rewriting copied code
  does not remove the obligation.

2.1 What you accept
  - Every version you publish through CREADDINSCART STUDIO carries the four
    conditions above, unchanged in meaning.
  - You do not remove, hide, shrink or restyle the attribution to make it
    illegible, and you do not move it behind a menu that is closed by default.
  - You do not present CREADDINSCART STUDIO as your own product and you do not
    rename it.
  - You keep the upstream licence of the project you edited, including its
    notice and source-availability terms (see Part 3).
  - Our code is credited at the point where you use it, even when it is one
    function and even when nothing is published.
  - You are responsible for what you publish: no secrets, no personal data,
    no code you have no right to redistribute.

2.2 What you keep
  - Copyright in your own edits.
  - Control of your GitHub repository, its visibility, its history and its
    releases.
  - The right to stop using CREADDINSCART STUDIO at any time. Versions already
    published keep their credit lines; nothing else is owed.

2.3 What CREADDINSCART STUDIO does not do
  - It does not take ownership of your repository or your code.
  - It does not relicense an upstream project. If the upstream licence is
    incompatible with your plan, the plan stops there.
  - It does not publish anything without your confirmation; a repository is
    only needed if you choose to push there.

2.4 Relationship to the upstream licence
  CREADDINSCART STUDIO adds attribution, not a new licence. It does not replace
  or override the MIT licence in Part 3; the MIT permissions, notice requirement
  and disclaimer remain in full force. A permissive upstream does not become
  stricter because CREADDINSCART STUDIO was used, and a commercial version is
  treated the same as a free one. If a condition is breached, that version is
  not licensed to use the CREADDINSCART STUDIO attribution and must be
  corrected or withdrawn; upstream licence obligations stand on their own and
  are unaffected by the breach.

